paras.en:
What a misfortune, although you are made
for fine and great deeds,
that this unjust fate of yours always
denies you encouragement and success;
that cheap habits stand in your way,
and pettiness, and indifference.

How will Artaxerxes give you these,
where will you find them in a satrapy;
and what life will you lead without them.
